        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>

<h2 id="how-to-pick">How to Pick from the Live Catalog</h2>

<ol>
    <li><strong>Open the live picker</strong> — AI Chat header → model dropdown, OR Daily Plans → AI Focus-Tune → "Models" button. Both hit <code>/ai2/providers</code> (chat) or <code>/api/focus/models</code> (daily plan) which return the live merged catalog.</li>
    <li><strong>Filter by <code>provider</code> and <code>price_tier</code></strong> — Each entry has:
        <ul>
            <li><code>provider</code>: <code>ollama</code> | <code>grok</code> | <code>openrouter</code></li>
            <li><code>price_tier</code>: <code>free</code> | <code>budget</code> | <code>standard</code> | <code>premium</code></li>
            <li><code>free</code>: boolean (true = no API cost)</li>
            <li><code>local</code>: boolean (true = runs on your Ollama host)</li>
            <li><code>price_prompt</code> / <code>price_completion</code>: USD per 1M tokens (when priced)</li>
        </ul>
    </li>
    <li><strong>Apply the task row above</strong> — Match your task to the "What to look for" column, then pick an available model from "Recommended models" that appears in the live list.</li>
    <li><strong>Prefer FREE first</strong> — If <code>nemotron-3-ultra-free</code> (OpenRouter) or your local Ollama models (<code>phi4:14b</code>, <code>llama3.1:8b</code>, <code>qwen2.5-coder</code>) are in the list, use them for budget/standard tasks. Save premium for planning and implementation.</li>
</ol>

<h2 id="provider-notes">Provider Notes (Comserv2 Specific)</h2>

<div class="doc-h3">OpenRouter (external, pay-per-token or free tier)</div>
<ul>
    <li>Models: <code>gpt-4o</code>, <code>gpt-4o-mini</code>, <code>claude-3.5-sonnet</code>, <code>claude-3.5-haiku</code>, <code>deepseek-coder-v2</code>, <code>deepseek-chat</code>, <code>nemotron-3-ultra-free</code>, <code>qwen2.5-coder</code>, etc.</li>
    <li>Free tier: <code>nemotron-3-ultra-free</code> — strong general model, no cost. <strong>OpenRouter does NOT auto-refill</strong> — when paid credits hit 0 (HTTP 402), the app falls back to free models or Ollama.</li>
    <li>Pricing shown in live catalog is per 1M tokens (prompt/completion separate).</li>
</ul>

<div class="doc-h3">xAI Grok (external, auto-fill pay-per-token)</div>
<ul>
    <li>Models: <code>grok-3</code>, <code>grok-3-mini</code>, etc.</li>
    <li>Auto-fills from linked payment method — no "quota API" to check remaining.</li>
    <li>Not free; use when you specifically want Grok's reasoning style.</li>
</ul>

<div class="doc-h3">Ollama (local, zero API cost)</div>
<ul>
    <li>Models: whatever you have pulled on the Ollama host (<code>phi4:14b</code>, <code>llama3.1:8b</code>, <code>qwen2.5-coder</code>, <code>nemotron3-ultra</code>, etc.)</li>
    <li><strong>Always free</strong> — runs on your hardware. No network latency for generation.</li>
    <li>Best for: high-volume budget tasks, code documentation (with <code>qwen2.5-coder</code>), offline work.</li>
    <li>IP/host selection is in the picker (not model dropdown) — <code>/ai</code> endpoint resolves Ollama host.</li>
</ul>

<div class="doc-h3">SuperGrok (prepaid OAuth, NOT the same as xAI API)</div>
<ul>
    <li>Prepaid subscription (OAuth token at <code>~/.comserv/secrets/supergrok_oauth</code>).</li>
    <li>No remaining-quota API — you won't see a balance in the picker.</li>
    <li>When exhausted, app falls back to OpenRouter free / Ollama.</li>
    <li>Token sync: <code>script/sync_supergrok_token.pl</code>.</li>
</ul>

<h2 id="anti-patterns">Anti-Patterns to Avoid</h2>

<table class="doc-table">
    <thead>
        <tr><th class="doc-th">Anti-pattern</th><th class="doc-th">Why it fails</th><th class="doc-th">Correct approach</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td class="doc-td">Hardcoding <code>gpt-4o</code> or <code>grok-3</code> as default</td>
            <td class="doc-td">Model may not be in live catalog (key expired, network down, not pulled)</td>
            <td class="doc-td">Use <code>ModelCatalog->default_for($c, page => '...')</code> — returns first live match</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td class="doc-td">Assuming OpenRouter free tier always works</td>
            <td class="doc-td">402 when credits empty; no auto-refill</td>
            <td class="doc-td">Always have Ollama models pulled as ultimate fallback</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td class="doc-td">Using premium model for changelogs/polishing</td>
            <td class="doc-td">Wastes budget on template-driven work</td>
            <td class="doc-td">Match model tier to task tier (table above)</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td class="doc-td">Ignoring <code>local</code> flag</td>
            <td class="doc-td">Ollama models need host reachable; picker shows IP selector separately</td>
            <td class="doc-td">Check host connectivity if Ollama models show but don't respond</td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>

<h2 id="quick-decision-flow">Quick Decision Flow</h2>

<pre class="doc-code">
TASK TYPE
    │
    ├─► Planning / Architecture / Master Plans
    │       └─► LIVE LIST → premium (gpt-4o, claude-3.5-sonnet, nemotron-3-ultra-free)
    │
    ├─► Code Documentation / Explaining Implementation
    │       └─► LIVE LIST → code-aware (deepseek-coder-v2, qwen2.5-coder, gpt-4o, phi4:14b)
    │
    ├─► Writing Code / Refactoring / Debugging
    │       └─► LIVE LIST → premium code (gpt-4o, claude-3.5-sonnet, deepseek-coder-v2)
    │
    ├─► Organizing / Restructuring / Indexing
    │       └─► LIVE LIST → standard/budget (gpt-4o-mini, deepseek-chat, llama3.1:8b)
    │
    ├─► Polishing / Wording / Style
    │       └─► LIVE LIST → standard writing (gpt-4o-mini, claude-3.5-haiku, nemotron-3-ultra-free)
    │
    └─► Changelogs / SUMMARY.md / Templates
            └─► LIVE LIST → budget (gpt-4o-mini, nemotron-3-ultra-free, phi4:14b)
</pre>

<h2 id="live-catalog-access">Accessing the Live Catalog Programmatically</h2>

<p>In Perl (Controller/Model):</p>
<pre class="doc-code">
use Comserv::Util::ModelCatalog;

# Get full live catalog (600s cached)
my $models = Comserv::Util::ModelCatalog->catalog($c);

# Get page-appropriate default (respects role filters)
my $default = Comserv::Util::ModelCatalog->default_for($c, page => 'documentation');
</pre>

<p>In JavaScript (browser):</p>
<pre class="doc-code">
// Chat header picker (model-select.js)
fetch('/ai2/providers', { headers: { 'X-Forwarded-For': '127.0.0.1' } })
  .then(r => r.json())
  .then(data => console.log(data.models)); // [{name, provider, label, price_tier, free, local, ...}]

// Daily Plan AI Focus-Tune
fetch('/api/focus/models', { headers: { 'X-Forwarded-For': '127.0.0.1' } })
  .then(r => r.json())
  .then(data => console.log(data.models));
</pre>

